It follows the catalog's `integrations.add_url_channel` pattern, the same shape as `add_msteams`. The view:
- needs a logged-in user and the `VICTOROPS_ENABLED` setting;
- gets the project through `_get_rw_project_for_user`, so only users with write access can add the integration;
- validates the URL with `forms.AddUrlForm`;
- creates a `victorops` channel, assigns all the project's checks to it, and redirects to `hc-channels`.

The pcat check found no high-severity deviations. It flagged only low-severity items, which are the changed setting name, kind and template name. It also listed `_get_project_for_user` from `views.py` as "added" code, but I didn't change that function.

There are two things to know:
- **Existing view:** `hc/integrations/victorops/views.py` already has `add_splunk_oncall`. It saves `request.POST["value"]` without validating it. The URL name `hc-add-victorops` is routed to a function called `views.add` in `hc/integrations/victorops/urls.py`, and that function doesn't exist in the file, so the route looks broken.
- **Not wired in:** the new view isn't connected to any URL yet. If you want it to replace the old view, change `hc/integrations/victorops/urls.py` to point `hc-add-victorops` at `hc.front.views.add_victorops`. I can make that change if you want.

